00:02:41.020 --> 00:02:47.780
Most people will maybe never make it out of the helicopter stuff, and that's why they let you skip to the ground mission if you're not so lucky.

00:02:47.780 --> 00:02:59.380
But, I don't know, like, that whole, like, plot of Johnny, Jimbo Baby, McGibbeth, and, you know, you've got to infiltrate these bases, and it's not taking itself seriously.

00:02:59.380 --> 00:03:05.300
It's actually kind of funny, but it just doesn't feel like it's matching well with the rest of the gameplay world.

00:03:05.540 --> 00:03:10.420
No, it's pretty, yeah, there's definitely two worlds here.

00:03:10.420 --> 00:03:29.820
There's the, again, like, with how goofball the story and framing stuff are, like, not only is he this, like, weird green guy in a mask, very classically cartoon villain in how he's illustrated,

00:03:29.820 --> 00:03:41.260
but it's also implying that he is the leader of a nation, like, a sovereign nation that has this kind of, like,

00:03:42.020 --> 00:03:52.380
like, oh, I would have gotten away with it if it wasn't for you meddling kids, but it's specifically McGibbeth's that always, like, foils his international plans.

00:03:52.380 --> 00:04:14.560
And then you go on to having to figure out the heading and the radio frequency to get your GPS synced, and you have to take into account wind, and it's, there's so, such weird juxtapositions between the game and everything else.

